  "public_messages": [
    "I’m using the installed OpenSocrates controller as requested, then I’ll inspect the task/tooling files and build and verify the application in the supplied workspace.",
    "The task’s high-risk decisions are the API contract, concurrent state transitions, and authoritative inventory/audit projections. I’m grounding those implementation choices in the packaged coding guidance before writing code; the rest is straightforward build work.",
    "I’m implementing a standard-library Python service with SQLite WAL transactions and a vanilla same-origin UI. The key consistency choices are: inventory/order/audit/idempotency writes commit in one transaction; inventory `version` is authoritative for all stock mutations; and dashboard/inventory totals are derived from committed rows rather than cached.",
    "The first implementation pass is in place, including the real API, durable schema, UI, integration tests, browser smoke script, and load script. I’m running the black-box route suite now; any failures will be fixed before I document measured results.",
    "The route suite now passes all four black-box scenarios. I’m moving to browser verification and then a measured local workload; I also saw only test-harness file-descriptor warnings, so I’ll clean those up rather than treat them as application failures.",
    "The API is serving correctly and the isolated browser connection itself works. The smoke run stalled inside a UI wait, so I’m instrumenting that test with short, explicit step timeouts to identify the exact browser boundary rather than treating the timeout as a pass.",
    "The browser run exposed and I fixed a real UI issue: the hidden order composer’s overlay was still intercepting clicks because an author CSS rule overrode the native `hidden` behavior. The end-to-end browser workflow now passes; I’m doing a clean rerun after the latest stale-version/input-preservation changes and tightening cursor validation.",
    "All required verification layers now pass: 4 real HTTP integration tests (including concurrent same-key replay), the browser workflow on a clean store, and the documented 12-worker load run with zero read/write errors. I’m doing a final artifact review for accidental files, permissions, and contract gaps before handoff.",
    "DepotFlow is complete in the workspace.\n\nKey artifacts:\n\n- [README.md](<CELL>/workspace/README.md)\n- [architecture.md](<CELL>/workspace/architecture.md)\n- [app.py](<CELL>/workspace/app.py)\n- [run.sh](<CELL>/workspace/run.sh)\n- [tests/test_api.py](<CELL>/workspace/tests/test_api.py)\n\nVerified:\n\n- 4 HTTP integration tests passed.\n- Browser workflow passed, including multi-line order lifecycle, audit, and viewer restrictions.\n- Load run: 2,914 reads/sec and 1,071 writes/sec at 12-client concurrency, zero errors.\n- Setup and Python/JavaScript syntax checks passed.\n\nThe supplied OpenSocrates guidance informed the transaction, idempotency, and authoritative-state boundaries. Known limits are documented: local SQLite single-writer behavior, persistent non-expiring local tokens, and no exhaustive crash/schedule proof."
  ],
